---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const LAYERS = [
  {
    num: '01',
    id: 'layer-1-execution',
    name: 'Execution & Sandboxing',
    critique:
      'Why build a bespoke deterministic host when WebAssembly (Wasmtime + WASI) already delivers capability-safe sandboxing, AOT/Cranelift speed, and deterministic instruction-fuel accounting?',
    cleanRoomTitle: 'Clean-Room Lab (~5,000 SLOC RCE Host)',
    cleanRoomBody:
      'Isolates a pure state-event fold P = (S, E, δ, D, λ) with SHA-256 log chaining and zero JIT background threads so replay determinism (10,500 streams × 6 targets, 0 mismatches) and log-hash overhead can be measured without runtime confounding. Already compiles to wasm32-wasip1.',
    bridgeTitle: 'Drop-In Standards Bridge: Wasmtime + WASI + Hardware/OS Shunts',
    bridgeBody:
      'Run untrusted or synthesized agent tools inside Wasmtime + WASI capability sandboxes with deterministic fuel enabled—paired with physical DC shunts (TI INA260 / INA3221 measured_j) or chip counters (Linux RAPL / Apple IOReport reported_j). Instruction fuel bounds logical op-count (halting infinite loops), whereas cache misses and runtime FP32 unpacking shift joules-per-op by up to 81.86× on silicon. The two meters are orthogonal complements, never rivals.',
    kitSlug: 'kits/standards-bridge/',
    links: [
      { label: 'Metered Commit Gates →', href: '/papers/gates/' },
      { label: 'SATB 5-Host Telemetry →', href: '/papers/satb-harness/' },
    ],
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    id: 'layer-2-verification',
    name: 'Formal Verification & Surface Languages',
    critique:
      'Why ask human engineers or LLMs—whose pretraining corpora contain billions of lines of Rust, Python, TypeScript, and Lean 4 but zero bespoke RCE—to author code in a custom surface syntax?',
    cleanRoomTitle: 'Clean-Room Lab (Nameless De Bruijn + 6-Kernel Lean 4.36.0 IR)',
    cleanRoomBody:
      'Keeps RCE strictly under the hood as a canonical nameless normal form (0/500 alpha-renaming cache collisions) whose core semantics (5,393 theorem constants) passes all 6 independent proof kernels of lake check --paranoid (lean4lean, nanoda, con-leche, con-ron, leanchecker --paranoid, and Lean v4.36.0).',
    bridgeTitle: 'Drop-In Standards Bridge: Rust + Verus, Dafny, Lean 4, Python & TypeScript',
    bridgeBody:
      'Keep authoring and prompting in mainstream high-resource languages—Rust + Verus, Dafny, Lean 4, Python, Go, or TypeScript. As The Language Constellation (/constellation/) demonstrates across 12,117 catalogued languages and 75 benchmarked tree-sitter grammars (267 in the live dataset), mainstream languages express the same 113 universal computational constructs with measured syntactic-sugar ratios (Python N/C = 1.77, Go 1.75, TypeScript 2.44, Rust 2.56, C++ 3.38, Lean 4.15). Canonical normalization belongs under the hood, not in the human editor.',
    kitSlug: 'kits/standards-bridge/',
    links: [
      { label: 'Explore /constellation/ (12,117 Languages) →', href: '/constellation/' },
      { label: 'RCE Compile Payback Horizon →', href: '/papers/rce-compile/' },
    ],
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    id: 'layer-3-spec-fidelity',
    name: "Specification Fidelity (Goodhart's Law Defense)",
    critique:
      "Under Goodhart's Law, if a microsecond gate C(z) ∈ {0, 1} checks weak example assertions or specs co-authored by the same LLM, won't the proposer game the spec with a trivial lookup table—while wasting 80 J retries on grammar rejections?",
    cleanRoomTitle: 'Clean-Room Lab (56-Program Table-Control Falsifier & Rule W-INT-2)',
    cleanRoomBody:
      'OpenIE explicitly registered and published this exact failure mode (/faq/#hq-5): rebuilding 56 example-only modules as hardcoded lookup tables passed 56/56 naive example checks while diverging off-sample, prompting rule W-INT-2 and mutation gate W-MUT-1 (catching up to Cunha 2026 on specification-coverage bottlenecks).',
    bridgeTitle: 'Drop-In Standards Bridge: Spec ⊥ Impl + Mutant/Vacuity Gates + llguidance/Outlines',
    bridgeBody:
      'Enforce three barriers in kits/spec-fidelity-barrier/: (1) Context-Isolated Specs (Spec ⊥ Impl)—the implementation agent cannot read held-out property seeds or edit the contract bundle; (2) Mutant & Vacuity Kill Gates—a spec is rejected before synthesis if it is vacuously satisfiable or fails to kill injected behavioral mutants; (3) In-Loop Grammar-Constrained Decoding (llguidance / Outlines)—masks invalid tokens during generation so 0 joules are wasted on syntax-error retries.',
    kitSlug: 'kits/spec-fidelity-barrier/',
    links: [
      { label: 'FAQ #5 Table-Control Falsifier →', href: '/faq/#hq-5' },
      { label: 'RCE-JEPA H15 & W-MUT-1 →', href: '/papers/rce-jepa/' },
    ],
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    id: 'layer-4-compilation',
    name: 'Downward Compilation & Skill Libraries',
    critique:
      'Why compile agent policies all the way down to raw FPGA LUT6 netlists when 95% of repeated software tasks are solved cleanly by verified code/skill libraries, and hardware synthesis already has LLVM MLIR + CIRCT?',
    cleanRoomTitle: 'Clean-Room Lab (KV260 xck26 LUT6 & Simon-Kadane Horizon)',
    cleanRoomBody:
      'Measures the physical floor on an AMD Kria KV260 (11.43 nJ/check TI INA260 measured_j) and openXC7 RTL to establish where sub-microjoule combinational gates pay back synthesis energy N* on extreme high-frequency edge loops.',
    bridgeTitle: 'Drop-In Standards Bridge: Stop at Rungs 1–3 (95% of Workloads); Lower Rung 4 via MLIR/CIRCT',
    bridgeBody:
      'Do not synthesize FPGA gates for everyday software! Stop at Rungs 1–3: Rung 1 Exact/Nameless Hash Lookup (~0.3–1.8 µJ), Rung 2 Synthesized Rust/Wasm Skill Routines (gate-admitted tool libraries), and Rung 3 compact 0.5B–2B packed-integer local models—capturing 16.7×–29.9× Zipf(0.85) energy cuts on commodity CPUs. For the <5% ultra-low-latency hardware edge, lower through LLVM MLIR + CIRCT (comb / hw dialects → SystemVerilog) paired with exhaustive/SMT translation validation.',
    kitSlug: 'kits/standards-bridge/',
    links: [
      { label: 'Compiled Agency 4-Stage Cascade →', href: '/living/compiled-agency/' },
      { label: 'Downward LUT6 & Horizon Math →', href: '/papers/lut-adapt/' },
    ],
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    id: 'layer-5-wire-telemetry',
    name: 'Wire Protocols & Energy Telemetry',
    critique:
      'Why introduce custom binary WAI1 envelopes or BSL-1.1 storage dependencies when production fleets already standardize on Apache-2.0 OpenTelemetry, FlatBuffers / Cap’n Proto, and IETF COSE cryptographic receipts?',
    cleanRoomTitle: 'Clean-Room Lab (34-Workload Wire & Tokenization Impedance Benchmark)',
    cleanRoomBody:
      'Quantifies why reparsing and retokenizing verbose UTF-8 JSON/Markdown transcripts across agent hops burns order-of-magnitude excess CPU/memory energy compared with zero-copy typed binary frames (/papers/ai-reads-human/).',
    bridgeTitle: 'Drop-In Standards Bridge: Apache-2.0 OpenTelemetry Joule Conventions + IETF COSE_Sign1 + FlatBuffers',
    bridgeBody:
      'Zero custom parser lock-in and 100% Apache-2.0 licensing. Emit standard OpenTelemetry spans and metrics carrying orthogonal joule attributes (openie.energy.measured_j, openie.energy.reported_j, openie.energy.est_j, openie.energy.evidence_class—never summed across classes!), serialize high-rate tool payloads in zero-copy FlatBuffers, and wrap Ed25519 + BLAKE3 provenance digests in standard IETF RFC 9052 COSE_Sign1 envelopes.',
    kitSlug: 'kits/standards-bridge/',
    links: [
      { label: '34-Workload Wire Benchmark →', href: '/papers/ai-reads-human/' },
      { label: 'Run All 9 Apache-2.0 Kits →', href: '/replication/' },
    ],
  },
];

const CLONE_SPEC_FIDELITY = `git clone https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments.git
cd openie-research-experiments/kits/spec-fidelity-barrier
./run_kit.sh`;

const CLONE_STANDARDS_BRIDGE = `git clone https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments.git
cd openie-research-experiments/kits/standards-bridge
./run_kit.sh`;

const OTEL_SCHEMA_SNIPPET = `{
  "name": "agent.tool.commit_gate",
  "attributes": {
    "openie.gate.verdict": "admitted",
    "openie.gate.spec_isolated": true,
    "openie.gate.mutant_kill_ratio": 0.984,
    "openie.cascade.rung": 2,
    "openie.cascade.surface": "wasmtime_wasi_skill",
    "openie.energy.evidence_class": "reported_j",
    "openie.energy.measured_j": null,
    "openie.energy.reported_j": 0.00177,
    "openie.energy.est_j": null,
    "openie.energy.sensor": "linux_powercap_rapl_pkg0",
    "openie.receipt.envelope": "ietf_rfc9052_cose_sign1",
    "openie.receipt.payload_codec": "flatbuffers",
    "openie.receipt.blake3": "a541323b9e0d418c2f1074c890e2b1d7f4e9c3a2180756b9d312e4f8c09a46f0"
  }
}`;

const ld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'Clean-Room Core vs. Drop-In Standards Bridge: Adopting Metered & Verified AI Without Reinventing Your Stack',
  url: 'https://research.openie.dev/standards/',
  description:
    '5-layer architecture guide mapping OpenIE clean-room verification research onto mainstream Apache-2.0 production standards: Rust + Verus, Lean 4, Wasmtime + WASI, llguidance/Outlines, LLVM MLIR + CIRCT, OpenTelemetry joule semantic conventions, and IETF RFC 9052 COSE_Sign1 + FlatBuffers.',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'David Charlot' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Open Interface Engineering, Inc.', url: 'https://openie.dev' },
  dateModified: '2026-11-28',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Clean-Room Core vs. Drop-In Standards Bridge: Adopting Metered & Verified AI Without Reinventing Your Stack"
  description="Adopt Metered & Verified AI today without reinventing your stack: a 5-layer architecture matrix and interactive stack recommender bridging OpenIE's clean-room lab to Rust, Lean 4/Verus, Wasmtime/WASI, llguidance/Outlines, MLIR/CIRCT, OpenTelemetry, and IETF COSE/FlatBuffers."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(ld)} />

  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-24">
    <!-- Top Epistemic & Licensing Badge Strip -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
      <span class="font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-brand-amber text-brand-dark font-bold">
        Architecture &amp; Interoperability Guide · 100% Apache-2.0 Bridge
      </span>
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-emerald-400/45 bg-emerald-500/12 text-emerald-300">
        Zero Custom Syntax or BSL-1.1 Lock-In Required
      </span>
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-brand-border text-brand-slate">
        measured_j ⊥ reported_j ⊥ est_j ⊥ unmetered
      </span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-5xl">
      Clean-Room Core vs. Drop-In Standards Bridge: <span class="text-brand-amber">Adopting Metered &amp; Verified AI Without Reinventing Your Stack</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base md:text-lg text-brand-slate leading-relaxed max-w-4xl">
      A candid engineering map answering the five toughest architectural questions about Open Interface Engineering&rsquo;s research: why our papers isolate minimal clean-room kernels to measure physical floors, and how production teams get the exact same safety gates, Zipfian lookup savings, and cryptographic joule receipts <strong class="text-brand-white">this week</strong> on top of <code class="text-brand-cyan">Rust</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">Lean 4</code> / <code class="text-brand-cyan">Verus</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">Wasmtime</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">MLIR/CIRCT</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">IETF COSE</code>, and <code class="text-brand-cyan">OpenTelemetry</code>.
    </p>

    <!-- DEPTH 1: PLAIN WORDS + EVERYDAY ANALOGY + AND-BUT-THEREFORE -->
    <div id="depth-plain" class="glass-card p-6 md:p-8 mt-8 border border-brand-amber/40 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-amber/[0.06] via-transparent to-brand-cyan/[0.05]">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-amber text-brand-dark font-bold">
          Depth 1 · Plain Story (2 min)
        </span>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-mono text-xs">
          <a href="/constellation/" class="text-brand-cyan no-underline hover:underline">
            Explore 12,117-Language Constellation →
          </a>
          <span class="text-brand-gray">·</span>
          <a href="/replication/" class="text-emerald-300 no-underline hover:underline">
            9 Standalone Apache-2.0 Kits →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Everyday Analogy Callout -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-cyan/35 bg-brand-cyan/[0.06] mb-5">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-brand-cyan font-semibold mb-1">
          💡 Everyday Analogy — Circuit Breakers &amp; Electric Meters Don&rsquo;t Require a New Wall Plug
        </div>
        <p class="font-body text-sm md:text-base text-brand-light leading-relaxed m-0">
          You don&rsquo;t need to build your own power grid or invent a new three-prong plug shape just to put a <strong class="text-brand-white">circuit breaker</strong> and an <strong class="text-brand-white">electric meter</strong> on your house. OpenIE&rsquo;s clean-room core isolates the physics inside a tiny ~5,000-line reference lab so every theorem and joule reading can be audited without hidden compiler noise—while our <code class="text-brand-cyan">Apache-2.0</code> <strong class="text-brand-amber">Standards Bridge</strong> snaps straight onto <code class="text-brand-cyan">Rust</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">Lean 4</code> / <code class="text-brand-cyan">Verus</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">WebAssembly</code> / <code class="text-brand-cyan">Wasmtime</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">MLIR</code> / <code class="text-brand-cyan">CIRCT</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">IETF COSE</code> / <code class="text-brand-cyan">FlatBuffers</code>, and <code class="text-brand-cyan">OpenTelemetry</code> today.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3-Beat And · But · Therefore Arc -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-emerald-300 font-bold mb-1">
            1 · Setup (And)
          </div>
          <p class="font-body text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed m-0">
            Modern engineering teams already run mature sandboxes (<code class="text-brand-cyan">Wasmtime</code>), verified contracts (<code class="text-brand-cyan">Verus</code>, <code class="text-brand-cyan">Lean 4</code>), compiler IRs (<code class="text-brand-cyan">MLIR</code>), and telemetry (<code class="text-brand-cyan">OpenTelemetry</code>)—and <a href="/constellation/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">/constellation/</a> shows how <strong class="text-brand-white">75 benchmarked tree-sitter grammars</strong> across <strong class="text-brand-white">12,117 languages</strong> already map onto the same <strong class="text-brand-white">113 universal constructs</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-brand-amber font-bold mb-1">
            2 · Tension (But)
          </div>
          <p class="font-body text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed m-0">
            Reading our clean-room papers in isolation can make it look as if adopting verified, joule-accounted AI requires rewriting code in raw <code class="text-brand-amber">RCE</code>, trusting naive LLM-written tests against <strong class="text-brand-white">Goodhart&rsquo;s Law</strong>, compiling Python to raw <code class="text-brand-amber">LUT6</code> gates, or adopting custom <code class="text-brand-amber">WAI1</code> frames. <strong class="text-brand-white">None of that lock-in is required.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-brand-cyan font-bold mb-1">
            3 · Resolution (Therefore)
          </div>
          <p class="font-body text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed m-0">
            Keep your mainstream languages, compilers, and observability pipeline. Add three drop-in <code class="text-brand-cyan">Apache-2.0</code> primitives: <strong class="text-brand-white">context-isolated mutant-killing gates</strong> (<code class="text-brand-cyan">Spec ⊥ Impl</code>), <strong class="text-brand-white">Rung 1–3 lookup/Wasm skill caching</strong>, and <strong class="text-brand-white">orthogonal OTel + COSE joule receipts</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DEPTH 2A: INTERACTIVE STACK RECOMMENDER (4 PRIORITY SLIDERS) -->
    <section id="stack-recommender" aria-labelledby="rec-heading" class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 md:p-8 border border-brand-cyan/35">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-cyan/20 text-brand-cyan font-semibold">
          Depth 2 · Interactive Stack Recommender
        </span>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5" role="group" aria-label="Workload presets">
          <button type="button" data-std-preset="85,95,15,25" class="std-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-brand-amber bg-brand-amber/15 text-brand-amber font-mono text-[11px] cursor-pointer">
            Preset: Ship This Week (SaaS / Agent API)
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-std-preset="60,85,20,75" class="std-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-brand-border text-brand-slate hover:text-brand-white font-mono text-[11px] cursor-pointer">
            High-Assurance Rust / FinTech
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-std-preset="45,65,95,55" class="std-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-brand-border text-brand-slate hover:text-brand-white font-mono text-[11px] cursor-pointer">
            Sub-mJ Robotics / FPGA Edge
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-std-preset="20,25,60,98" class="std-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-brand-border text-brand-slate hover:text-brand-white font-mono text-[11px] cursor-pointer">
            Clean-Room 6-Kernel Proof Audit
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="rec-heading" class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-white m-0">
        Dial Your Team&rsquo;s Constraints — Get Your Recommended 5-Layer Stack
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate max-w-3xl">
        Move the four priority sliders below. The recommender computes the lowest-friction combination across sandboxing, surface languages, Goodhart-resistant specs, cascade compilation rungs, and telemetry envelopes.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mt-6">
        <label class="block p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center font-mono text-xs mb-2">
            <span class="text-brand-white font-semibold">1. Production Velocity (Ship This Week)</span>
            <span id="val-velocity" class="text-brand-amber font-bold">85%</span>
          </div>
          <input id="sl-velocity" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="85" class="w-full accent-amber-400 cursor-pointer" />
          <span class="block mt-1 font-body text-[11.5px] text-brand-gray">High favors zero-migration drop-in wrappers around existing CI and model endpoints.</span>
        </label>

        <label class="block p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center font-mono text-xs mb-2">
            <span class="text-brand-white font-semibold">2. Existing Toolchain Compatibility</span>
            <span id="val-compat" class="text-brand-cyan font-bold">95%</span>
          </div>
          <input id="sl-compat" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="95" class="w-full accent-teal-400 cursor-pointer" />
          <span class="block mt-1 font-body text-[11.5px] text-brand-gray">High keeps Rust/Python/TS, Wasmtime, MLIR/LLVM, and existing OpenTelemetry collectors untouched.</span>
        </label>

        <label class="block p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center font-mono text-xs mb-2">
            <span class="text-brand-white font-semibold">3. Sub-Millijoule Edge / FPGA Target</span>
            <span id="val-edge" class="text-emerald-300 font-bold">15%</span>
          </div>
          <input id="sl-edge" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="15" class="w-full accent-emerald-400 cursor-pointer" />
          <span class="block mt-1 font-body text-[11.5px] text-brand-gray">Low stops at CPU/Wasm Rungs 1–3; high activates packed-int SIMD or MLIR/CIRCT → SystemVerilog hardware lowering.</span>
        </label>

        <label class="block p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-dark/55">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center font-mono text-xs mb-2">
            <span class="text-brand-white font-semibold">4. Cross-Layer Mechanized Proof Minimalism</span>
            <span id="val-proof" class="text-brand-indigo font-bold">25%</span>
          </div>
          <input id="sl-proof" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="25" class="w-full accent-indigo-400 cursor-pointer" />
          <span class="block mt-1 font-body text-[11.5px] text-brand-gray">Moderate uses property + mutant gates or Verus/Dafny; extreme adds 6-kernel Lean 4.36.0 &amp; nameless RCE equivalence.</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <!-- Dynamic Output Card -->
      <div class="mt-6 p-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-amber/40 bg-brand-dark/80">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 pb-3 border-b border-brand-border">
          <div>
            <div class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-brand-amber font-semibold">
              Recommended Architecture Profile
            </div>
            <h3 id="rec-profile-title" class="font-display text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-brand-white m-0 mt-0.5">
              Drop-In Production Standards Bridge (Rungs 1–3 · Zero Custom Lock-In)
            </h3>
          </div>
          <span id="rec-ramp-badge" class="font-mono text-xs px-3 py-1 rounded-md border border-emerald-400/45 bg-emerald-500/12 text-emerald-300">
            Est. Integration: 1–3 Days · 100% Apache-2.0
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-3 mt-4" id="rec-layers-grid">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white/[0.02]">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-brand-amber">1 · Sandbox &amp; Meter</div>
            <div id="rec-l1" class="font-display text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-brand-white mt-1">Wasmtime + WASI fuel + RAPL / IOReport reported_j</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white/[0.02]">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-brand-cyan">2 · Surface &amp; Proofs</div>
            <div id="rec-l2" class="font-display text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-brand-white mt-1">Mainstream Rust / Python / TS + Property Contracts</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white/[0.02]">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-emerald-300">3 · Spec Fidelity</div>
            <div id="rec-l3" class="font-display text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-brand-white mt-1">Spec ⊥ Impl Isolation + Mutant Gate + Outlines/llguidance</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white/[0.02]">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-brand-amber">4 · Cascade Rung</div>
            <div id="rec-l4" class="font-display text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-brand-white mt-1">Stop at Rungs 1–3 (Hash Lookup → Wasm Skills → 0.5B–2B Local)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white/[0.02]">
